Z||000012||Mach10||08-30-2001||02:15 PM||||Turbo, built 2.8. Initial assesments figure on ~200hp, little weight gain, and reasonably cheap (expensive part is rebuilding the 2.8).<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000013||Spektyr||08-30-2001||02:23 PM||||Personally I think it would be wise for me to avoid the hairdryer.  Partly because of the nightmares I've heard of getting them to run properly, and then partly due to me really not wanting the car to be 'moody'.<P>If the oil isn't perfect in most cars, they just deal with it till the next oil change.<P>Turbos however tend to commit hari-kari if their oil isn't nice and pretty.<P>My Fiero has to be fun, or I won't drive it.  If I have to constantly be poking at the motor just to keep it running right... well that's not as much fun.<P>I enjoy working on cars, but if I wanted something that was going to break constantly I'd get a pre-Ford Jaguar.  Which isn't to say that turbos are especially break-down prone.  It's just that they're something I'm not especially knowledgable about, and they add a bunch of moving parts.  Moving parts break, and turbo parts are $$$.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Mach10||08-30-2001||02:41 PM||||I am so anal about my oil, it isn't funny. I change it every 3k or so, 'Cos I know that my engine will last forever if I do. Besides, my mechanic has an ongoing special: 12CDN for a full change and filter. Takes 15 minutes, I'm gone. Costs exactly 2.00 more than doing it myself.<P>I'm thinking of ways to deal with the excess heat. Probably will involve some of the air blowers I have lying around. I've got a nifty idea, we'll see how it pans out.<P>I'd LIKE to do an intercooler, but that may be difficult...<P>EDIT: <BR>Just caught that, spektyr: I happen to OWN a pre-ford Jaguar. It doesn't break that often. Yeah, it's not running right now due to a bad tranny that we haven't the time/resources to fix.<BR>God, I'd LOVE to have that Jag DOHC 6 shreiking like a rabid cougar behind my head. Might be a little big though... *sigh*<BR>Anyone wanna help me design a mounting plate for a '75 4.2L Jaguar Flat-6?<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 08-30-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000015||GTMike||08-30-2001||11:52 PM||||these are my planns.  since i'm a poor student  i'm going with the the 3.4 pushrod.<BR>you can get one for around 550 bucks and around 50k miles.    when i do get mine i'm going to throw some forged pistens in it. and a cam. i'm going to keep my compression low  because  i'll be adding a turbo. later on.    with bigger injectors and a fule pressure regulator i should be able to supply enough fule any one know what 3.4 v6 with 10psi turbo would do in a 1/4 mile.  i would say 13s easy   i'm hopeing for 250hp with the 10psi.   later on when i learn more i want to crank up the psi to around 15psi shooting for 11s at sea level<BR>||||reg||1
